From 815825dfbb3443ce86482a64351823e69f588565 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ththeod <2376818+ththeod@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:35:45 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 114/138] VLLM_EXP_SKINNY_SM86=1: Triton skinny decode GEMM for
 sm_86 (3090) bf16 linears

Decode/verify GEMMs (8-64 rows) are memory-bound; cuBLAS picked 16x16 wmma and
split-K + reduce kernels at ~2.7x the bandwidth floor (W12 profile). One program
per (N tile, K split), tensor-core dot with M padded; split-K partials are summed
in fixed order by the last-arriving split (per-tile counter, reset in-kernel):
deterministic, one launch. Per-layer scratch slots. Plans per local (N, K) and
M bucket from VLLM_EXP_SKINNY_SM86_PLANS (tuned by /opt/flash-next/skinny/bench.py,
kept only where >= 5% faster than cuBLAS); everything else keeps F.linear.

Hooked into enable_qwen4_exp_low_latency_gemm (target model) and the DFlash 2
drafter. Both env vars are registered in envs.py so they enter the compile/AOT
cache key. apply() always calls the op: a token-count test there is evaluated
once at trace time and baked the fallback into the compiled graph (W20/W21).
CPU/meta weights (PLE offload process) are skipped.

W22 (p3b config, 16 slots): greedy single-request decode +9/+16/+10%
(code/prose/count), prefill unchanged, 2-12 requests +6-18%, 16 requests flat;
per-step compute at N=1 24.0 -> 20.7 ms. NaN poke clean, probes 8/8, GSM8K 97.0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
